<math id="S5.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+T</annotation></semantics></math> reports results with full temperature scaling.
<math id="S5.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+Ours" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+Ours</annotation></semantics></math> denotes our efficient temperature-scaling method.
<math id="S5.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta C</annotation></semantics></math> shows the reduction in computation cost relative to full temperature scaling.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
